From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:29:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 58% of the judge's docket is rebuilt from scratch every pass
 because the failure was never banked

MEASURED on the box 2026-09-24, from the judge's own report: of 140,090 cells submitted to the
pre-warm pool, 81,588 (58.2%) return NOT_RUN_BUILD_FAILED -- "signal construction returned no
executable cell" -- and all 81,588 are submitted again on the next pass. Work redone because its
result was never made durable: the same defect shape as the HMM cache that flushed only on the
last line of build(), and as the judge discarding 65 passing cells on a stop.

THE MECHANISM ALREADY EXISTED AND THE HARVEST WAS BLIND TO THIS CLASS. `judge_coverage` banks
unrunnable specs in data/hypotheses/unrunnable_specs.json (69,401 rows today), and
`order_docket` -- which `merge_hypotheses` calls as the last thing before writing the file the
sealed judge reads -- filters the docket by that bank with no special-casing of the reason. But
`name_unknowns` only names verdicts carrying `unmeasured`, and a build failure carries
`downstream_status` instead, so this class was never named and never parked. Nothing new is
built here: the bank, the filter and the re-open condition are the desk's own.

TWO RE-OPEN CONDITIONS, because one was not enough. Bar growth was already there, and it is now
read on the CELL'S OWN CHART (`_bar_bytes(sym, timeframe)`, timeframe taken from the judge's own
`SYM@TF.family.p=` cell id) -- re-admitting an M5 cell because the H1 frame grew is a different
symbol's answer. And a build failure is a fact about `families.family_<name>` as much as about
the bars, so each parked row carries a fingerprint of the family modules and goes back to the
judge the moment that code changes. Without it a fix to a family would leave every cell it would
now build parked for ever: a permanently-cached failure that should have become a pass, strictly
worse than the waste it saves.

IT CANNOT MOVE A GATE. A build failure is NOT_RUN -- never a pass, never a fail -- so it carries
no trial: the report shows n_trials 109 against 140,090 verdicts. Filtering it changes what the
judge REBUILDS, never what it judges or the bar it judges against. `missing_bars` is named and
deliberately NOT parked: that belongs to the conversion organ's bar supply.

Measured invalidation sanity before shipping: across all 69,401 existing bank rows, bar file
sizes were byte-stable hour to hour (grew=0, same=69,401), so the bank bites instead of flushing
itself every pass.

